# Architect 2.0 — server configuration. Copy to .env.local (gitignored) for local work.
# Every variable here is read on the server only. Never prefix one with NEXT_PUBLIC_, and never commit real values.
# docs/DEPLOYMENT.md walks through each of the three setups below.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Local demo (no credentials). Leave this file as it is: Architect runs on an in-process database with recorded
#    models, so the key demo reproduces exactly and offline.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Database. Empty = in-process PGlite, created and migrated from scratch on every start (local development only).
# Set it to a Postgres connection string to persist; for Supabase use the pooled one (transaction pooler, port 6543).
DATABASE_URL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Local, real models. Set ANTHROPIC_API_KEY and uncomment the two modes below.
#    Model names come from the agent configurations and the variables here — never from the UI.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is needed for the default live models; OPENAI_API_KEY only for an "openai:" model.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Agents run on the provider model in each AgentVersion instead of the deterministic fixture model.
# ARCHITECT_MODEL_MODE=live
# Architect drafts changes and rule changes with a real model instead of replaying the scripted demo edits.
# ARCHITECT_PROPOSER=live
# Judge assertions are scored instead of reported as skipped (implied by ARCHITECT_MODEL_MODE=live).
# ARCHITECT_JUDGE=live

# Optional model overrides (provider:model). Defaults: anthropic:claude-opus-5-5.
# ARCHITECT_PROPOSER_MODEL=anthropic:claude-opus-5-5
# JUDGE_MODEL=anthropic:claude-opus-5-5

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Production (Vercel). Set DATABASE_URL + ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, and set both modes to live explicitly.
#    A deployment without DATABASE_URL is refused, because each instance would keep its own throwaway copy of the
#    project. Accept that for a throwaway preview with ARCHITECT_ALLOW_EPHEMERAL_DB=1.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ARCHITECT_ALLOW_EPHEMERAL_DB=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Ship to GitHub (optional; everything else works without it). Server-side only: never prefix with NEXT_PUBLIC_.
# Prototype credential: a fine-grained personal access token limited to the repositories below, with
# Repository permissions → Contents: Read and write, Pull requests: Read and write. Production uses a GitHub App
# installation token instead (see docs/architecture.md).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ARCHITECT_GITHUB_TOKEN=
# Comma-separated owner/name allowlist the workspace may ship to (each needs at least one commit, e.g. a README).
# ARCHITECT_GITHUB_REPOS=your-org/laptop-advisor-agents
# Optional: where this workspace is reachable, so the PR links back to the change (…/?change=<id>).
# ARCHITECT_PUBLIC_URL=http://localhost:3000
# Optional: GitHub Enterprise Server API URL (default https://api.github.com).
# ARCHITECT_GITHUB_API_URL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Sign in with Google (optional). Both unset: Architect runs without accounts, every project is reachable, and the
# deterministic demo is unaffected. Set both and projects become owned by the Google account that created them.
# Supabase Auth on the same project as DATABASE_URL — no second provider, no user table of Architect's own.
#
# Setup, once:
#   1. Google Cloud console → APIs & Services → Credentials → OAuth client ID (Web application).
#      Authorized redirect URI: https://<project-ref>.supabase.co/auth/v1/callback
#   2. Supabase dashboard → Authentication → Providers → Google: paste the client ID and secret, enable.
#   3. Supabase dashboard → Authentication → URL Configuration:
#      Site URL        = your deployed origin (e.g. https://architect.example)
#      Redirect URLs   = https://architect.example/auth/callback  and  http://localhost:3000/auth/callback
#   4. Set the two variables below (Project settings → API). The anon key is safe to hold server-side; this app
#      never ships it to the browser.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# SUPABASE_URL=https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
# SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
# Required in production so the OAuth redirect can't be rewritten by a proxy header.
# ARCHITECT_PUBLIC_URL=https://architect.example
